      "text": "(\n    <div style={{ backgroundColor: 'var(--color-background)', boxSizing: 'border-box', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', fontSize: '12px', fontSynthesis: 'none', gap: '40px', height: 'fit-content', lineHeight: '16px', MozOsxFontSmoothing: 'grayscale', overflow: 'clip', overflowWrap: 'anywhere', padding: '48px', WebkitFontSmoothing: 'antialiased', width: '1800px' }}>\n      <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: '8px' }}>\n        <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'var(--color-foreground)', fontFamily: '\"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif', fontSize: '30px', fontWeight: 600, letterSpacing: '-0.025em', lineHeight: '36px' }}>\n          PayStep\n        </div>\n        <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'var(--color-muted-foreground)', fontFamily: '\"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif', fontSize: '16px', lineHeight: '24px', whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap', width: '900px' }}>\n          Under review, not yet approved. New design, built from the Boost screens.<br />One payment step for everything the app sells or funds: Boost now, and handles, songs and videos later (Spec 012 keeps paid handles disabled for now).<br />What each purchase supplies: the rows above From on Review, the amount, the address the server says to pay, and its own final message in place of Paid. Everything else is shared: Confirm, the From and Fee rows, the Pay button, Sending, and the two problem screens.<br />How it pays, from the code and Specs 004 and 014. The money moves from the persona's own wallet to platform custody as one USDC transfer that the wallet signs in the browser; the server only watches the chain. From names that persona and the short wallet address. Confirm appears only when the wallet is locked: a short sign-in, an email code in this sketch, unlocks it for five minutes, and then Review loads the balance and the fee.<br />Paying from an external address is not in version one. A person who holds funds elsewhere sends them to this wallet's address first (Wallet, Receive), which is what Add USDC opens. Paying straight from an external wallet would need the server to accept another payer, and I read Spec 014 as treating a wallet that links a persona to something else as a privacy problem, so it is a later decision. The From row is where a choice would go.<br />The fee is paid in ETH from the same wallet, so a wallet with USDC and no ETH cannot pay. Can't pay the fee exists only if the app does not cover the fee. Covering it, as the winnings send does with its gas top-up, is the better answer and removes that screen and the Fee row; the workspace_owner has not decided.<br />After Pay: Sending, then the purchase's own result. A failure that says nothing was sent offers another try. Not drawn: the wallet may have sent it and the status is unknown, the transfer reverted, and the five minutes running out; the code handles all three in text today.<br />Testnet only today: the transfer is Base Sepolia test USDC. Mainnet is separate work.<br />Source: api/reward-wallet-session.ts; features/rewards (reward-funding-panel, reward-sponsor-dialog); features/wallet (receive and send sheets); Specs 004, 012 §5.3.7 and 014.\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: '16px', width: '1704px' }}>\n        <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', color: 'var(--color-muted-foreground)', fontFamily: '\"Inter\", system-ui, sans-serif', fontSize: '16px', fontWeight: 500, letterSpacing: '0.03em', lineHeight: '24px', textTransform: 'uppercase', whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap' }}>\n          Phone: confirm, review, sending, paid<br />Problems: not enough USDC, cannot pay the fee\n        </div>\n        <div style={{ boxSizing: 'border-box', columnGap: '32px', display: 'flex', flexWrap: 'wrap', rowGap: '48px', width: '1704px' }}>\n          <div style={{ backgroundColor: 'var(--color-background)', borderColor: 'var(--color-